sentences.l:
I wronged the servants (of God) and roamed the lands, * and spent my lifetime in the drinking of the wines;
and I waded the torrents for the filching of the horses, * and the demolishing of the dwelling-ruins by the doing of the abominable;
and my affair (is) mighty and my crime (is) massive, * and Qātūl, of me (?), (is) the completion of the affairs.
And I hoped that I (would) attain the wishes * by that horse, but my journeying grew-exhausted;
and the length of the life I filch the horses, * and my death has-come before the All-Powerful;
and the last of my affair (is) that I toiled * for the provision of the stranger, the orphan, the poor.

sentences.i:
I wronged God’s servants and roamed through the lands, and wasted my days in the drinking of wine;
I forded the floods to make off with men’s horses, and laid homes in ruins with deeds of the vilest;
my case is a grave one, my guilt is enormous, and Qātūl was the crown of all my affairs.
I hoped through that horse to attain my desires, but my road failed beneath me;
all my life I was stealing horses, and now my death has come before the Almighty;
and the end of my story: I toiled and grew weary to give his living to a poor orphan stranger.
